WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:10.740
Strontium is an element that really came into
the news in the 1950s and 1960s because it’s

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:19.760
generated as the by product of the testing
of atomic bombs. Now human bones contain calcium

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:26.279
and the chemistry of strontium is very similar
to that of calcium and when atomic bombs went

00:00:26.279 --> 00:00:35.510
off, they released the radioactive isotope,
that’s a radioactive form of strontium known

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:45.469
as strontium-90, and it became so widely dispersed
around the world that people’s bones, children’s

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:51.469
teeth and so on, became mildly radioactive
through the formation of strontium-90. So

00:00:51.469 --> 00:01:02.460
it suddenly got this rather threatening aspect
which before, it was probably a slightly boring

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:10.150
element that nobody knew about. And now again
strontium-90 has gone away from the news,

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:14.290
no longer does it feature in pop songs, protest
songs and so on.

